WEBVTT

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:25.590
This bar has been letting me
perform since I started the band.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.030
I guess I like to play here,
compared with other places.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.260
Please tell me about the
characteristics of Sekiria.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.030
I don't know about that.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.430
When do you create songs?

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:45.250
Often while I'm riding my bike.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.340
Please give some comments to your fans.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.380
If you want to hear us,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:55.510
try coming to the Outside Ward.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:05.560
Overflowing lives on the outstretched Earth

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:15.400
Among the floating clouds, light is whispering

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.640
Even after a thousand years

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:28.980
The source, though it seems like
it's made of glass, works

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.580
Did you find the octagonal screwdriver?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.720
Are you going to be finished soon?

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.160
I'm sorry! It took a long time to find this.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.630
Oh, Priss.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.940
I thought you didn't use any assistants, Nigel.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.070
Uh, I...

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.710
It has nothing to do with what I think.

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:58.740
It's the fact that he found the
place where he's comfortable.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.050
Excuse me...

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.290
Are those the gaskets?

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.620
Yes! I brought them.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:16.600
Right.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.290
Tighten the bolt with the octagon.
Don't use too much torque.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.840
Yes, Sir.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:39.620
After you do it, I'd never need
another word from you

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.890
As if my soul were carried away

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:52.260
I feel myself drawn into a love that
doesn't seem friendly

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:03.380
Cheap negotiations made
while I was sleeping

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:06.880
I hide behind a lonely veil

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.520
I become an expert at love

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:23.930
In dull conversations, the wall
of words disturbs me Day by day

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:30.740
Hot looks released from honest eyes

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.040
Unadorned romanticism at
the bottom of your heart,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:43.010
I want to be drawn into a love
that doesn't seem friendly

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:29.890
Geez, she'll turn him down flat
because she's a normal girl.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.300
Why doesn't this guy give
me a speeding ticket?

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.810
You were about to say that, weren't you?

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.440
Do the AD Police work for
Traffic Enforcement now?

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.250
No way!

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.840
First of all, I don't have any tickets to give out.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.920
What do you want?

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.620
You're Priss Asagiri.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.110
I can call you Priss, can't I?

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.430
I'm Leon McNichol.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.000
I used to be a highway patrolman
in the normal police force.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.040
I miss those days when I chased
crazy bikers like you, Priss.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.110
I don't have time to listen
to a boring old story.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.470
You hate the AD Police, don't you?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:23.620
Well, I don't expect the citizens
to love us anyway.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.620
But are we doing something that
should make us hated?

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.380
We? What do you mean "we"?

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.260
With a police badge on, you think you're all alike.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.560
Guilty or honorable, you're all the same.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.120
I didn't mean that...

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.670
You rank lower than a bug.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.730
I have no intentions of ever being your friend.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.250
How pitiful!

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:57.380
Shut up, Daley! You jerk!

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.140
You came home late, didn't you?

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.840
I'm sorry!

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.850
That outfit looks good on you.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.620
Do you like it?

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.640
Yes, very much!

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:34.890
There's an oil stain on your face.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.080
I lied.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:51.140
You've been going to Nigel's place, haven't you?

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:55.440
The hard suits are done, so I
wonder what he's doing now?

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.580
Well, he's making a bike.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.620
A bike? How interesting.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.180
It's not an ordinary bike!

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.750
I don't understand it well, but it's incredible!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.790
He's creating the engine like it's a work of art!

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:13.030
It's not just the power. The engine
responds so delicately too!

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:16.360
I don't think ordinary people could
operate a machine like that.

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:19.530
I'm pretty sure that he's making it for Priss.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.070
For Priss?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.540
She has an unusual personality,

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:26.100
but it's a lot like Nigel's.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.080
Neither of them talk much, and
both of them love machines.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.070
I feel like they're communicating somehow.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.320
You must be quiet during meals.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:47.160
I'm sorry.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.230
Sylia?

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:54.330
I wasn't like this before.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.330
I like you, Sylia.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:03.280
I like you just as I did when we
lived together so long ago.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:10.520
I thought if I came here, I could
live with you the same as before.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.650
Yes, nothing's changed. It's just like before!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.020
I found out I was wrong.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.720
I'm the only one unchanged.
I knew things like that...

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.690
Mackey...

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.700
I'm going to live with Nigel.

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:56.100
Hi, Priss! Tonight, Linna is going
to spend the night with me.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:59.670
Why don't you join us? Linna told
me that she wants to see you.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:03.000
Of course, presents will be
welcome for our sweet tooth!

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:19.380
Mornings by myself, alone without you...

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.610
My god! What the hell is this room?!

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:45.250
Leave me alone! I like it this way.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:47.680
This isn't a room for a girl!

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:51.920
What? Are you still eating?

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.050
I can't stop.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.360
Oh, mail from Priss.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.860
What does she say?

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:04.230
If we go to Hot Legs, we can see her.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.700
"But pay the admission properly," she says.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:12.630
That's what I told you. Priss seems
like she loves to be alone.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:18.010
I see, but I don't understand
someone who never feels lonely.

00:11:18.010 --> 00:11:20.410
Oh, maybe she has a boyfriend?

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.880
You mean Priss?

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.720
Absolutely no way!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.220
I don't believe it, but maybe she's a...

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.390
What? What do you mean?

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:32.380
She likes women, maybe?

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.190
You're strange, Linna!

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.040
I don't know very much about her, but...

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.100
She used to love a man.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.070
Then what?

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:49.410
I think that he died.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:50.310
How?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:55.680
Don't know. But I've heard that's
why she's singing in the band.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.580
Oh, you can't say anything to Priss
about what I just told you! Right?

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:01.980
I know!

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.890
What do you think about the present world?

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.070
If you weren't a singer, what would you do?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.710
I'd be a Knight Saber and get a little rowdy.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:25.080
What does singing mean for you?

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:30.750
To confirm my... To confirm
that I am here and alive.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:31.720
I guess.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:51.800
Holding my square head, I can't
go to the places I want to go

00:12:56.140 --> 00:13:03.840
I already hung up the phone and
if I hang up my mind...

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:17.130
A mad boomer is loose in the KS
area. All available units respond.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:18.730
Right!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:24.400
Passion exists only in dreams

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:29.710
It's useless to breathe if you live
by common sense alone

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.140
Hey, Linna! Wake up!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:23.930
Excuse me, but if you don't drive
safely, I can't change my clothes.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:28.560
I'm sorry, but the fleeing boomer
is moving incredibly fast.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:30.670
Where is Priss?

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.510
We haven't been able to contact her.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.640
It can't be helped. You two go today.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.700
Sure.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:48.520
Damn, we can't catch up with it at all.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:51.120
It'll be bad if the boomer enters town.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:53.850
It'll crash into something, and
then there'll be a tragedy.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.200
Nene, we're gonna stop it by
attacking it from both sides.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.670
Okay!

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:12.740
Take this!

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.520
Nene!

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.330
What's that?! We're no match for it!

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.560
Because of the differences in mass.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:31.430
Sylia, hurry up and come to Nigel's shop!

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.400
What's the matter?

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.730
We're gonna use the machine
that Nigel's been making.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:35.970
What is it?

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:38.600
It's a Motoslave. It's not an ordinary bike.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.940
It should support the speed of the hard suit.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.610
But Linna and Nene aren't able to use that.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.640
Priss is on her way here now.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.540
Priss is? I understand.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.360
One more time!

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:09.030
It won't stop at all!

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:12.940
Damn you!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:19.350
We haven't even tried it out, so
don't give it too much power.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:23.280
If you control it well, it's possible
to catch up with that boomer.

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:25.450
I understand. Thank you, Mackey.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.120
Sure, Priss.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.120
Let's go, Priss.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.960
We're going where the mad
boomer will be in ten minutes.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.260
We're going to get there first.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.230
Okay.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.930
Are you ready, Priss?

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:43.400
Any time!

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.070
Rock and roll!

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:01.820
The Motoslave will sense the
conditions at all times

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:04.920
and feedback the best position to the hard suit.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.360
Feedback?

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:09.030
For example, the shape will
transform into the aero-body

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.830
by sensing the speed at the moment.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.670
Its shape will change and
combine with the hard suit.

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:17.430
I see. I don't think I understand
it well, but it sounds like fun.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.710
I can't do this any longer!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:26.910
Damn!

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.320
Linna, Nene, break away immediately.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.920
Priss is going to ram it.

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:31.980
Priss is?

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.470
She's really going to crash into it!

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:49.640
Priss, you're going too fast!

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:53.070
I know Nigel wouldn't make a
machine that couldn't survive this!

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:45.760
Go!

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:14.550
If there is nobody close to me,

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:20.420
My heart will disappear, so

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:25.060
I wander amid the noise of the city

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:30.050
And look for my love

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:52.550
1, 2...

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:56.280
1, 2, 3, 4...

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:59.530
Next Episode

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:04.570
Boomers are disappearing in the
outlying areas one by one.

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.530
There are lots of rumors about it.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.870
We receive breaking news about
a mad boomer appearing,

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.710
and we rush to the site.

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:13.070
It suddenly shows up right in front of us.

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:14.880
Right! I'm gonna do it this time!

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:17.880
I won't let Priss say I'm someone
who gets in her way!

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:20.580
I can do it! I can do it!

00:21:20.580 --> 00:21:22.480
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
